[Music]  in most zelda games the world map would  fill in automatically as you entered new  areas but even prior to breath the wild  some games like maduro's mask and the  wind waker already experimented with  different methods to uncover the map  gradually in this case through npcs who  are designed in a way that they stand  out and are easy to spot from a distance  the shika towers essentially served a  similar purpose with the added bonus of  acting as a fast travel point and due to  their size and the fact that they emit  an orange or blue glow they catch your  attention from pretty much anywhere on  the map when it comes to the sequel to  breath of the wild the footage we've  seen so far shows that the shika towers  as well as the shrines and the divine  beasts seem to be a thing of the past  even the sheikah slate has eluded us so  far causing many including myself to  believe that link's new spectral arm  will serve as the replacement for  hyrule's first smartphone at least when  it comes to link's new abilities but the  shika slate also doubled as the game's  excuse for the map and fast travel  mechanic as of right now we don't know  if we need to unlock the map of the  surface all over again in the sequel or  if this will only be reserved for new  areas like the sky and the underground  many have theorized about regardless if  the towers and shrines are truly gone  there needs to be at the very least a  new system that can replace breath the  wild's map function as well as its fast  travel points which were conveniently  spaced out all across hyrule which  brings us to the zone  [Music]  as much as the zone i have become a meme  in the zelda community at this point it  doesn't change the fact that there's  still plenty of reasons to believe that  something related to them will play a  role in breath of the wild too whether  it's the abundance of zonai architecture  seen in the first teaser the dragon head  mounted on link's shield and even the  green glowing arm could very well be  connected to them in some way still to  make the video more bearable for some of  you and to distract you from the fact  that this is a zonai related theory i  will mostly refer to them as the  backstreet boys for the remainder of the  video because similar to the zonai they  too are a relic of an age long forgotten  and if you're wondering why i own one of  their cds well it's because  shut up i just do alright let's not get  into details here despite that  disappearance the backstreet boys left  behind a lot of interesting architecture  and one of them in particular could be  of more significance in the sequel that  being the towers there's something very  peculiar about these structures not just  the fact that we know next to nothing  about them but if you've read creating a  champion you'll find that the towers we  see in breath of the wild weren't  actually supposed to look like this  instead of stark and basic columns the  original designs all feature a prevalent  and stylish dragon motif similar to some  of the other structures like the mazes  and some of their statues what's even  more interesting and equally confusing  is that the in-game version of the  towers have decorations on them that are  not consistent with the barbarians of  farren and thanks to the efforts of  others like lorulian historian it has  since come to light that these ornaments  are linked to the hylians instead if you  visit hyrule castle more specifically  the hallway leading to ganon's cocoon  you'll find pillars that have identical  decorations on them the overall design  of some of the pillars is also quite  similar to the towers a hexagonal shaped  column which gets wider at the very top  this has led some to believe that the  towers are actually supposed to be  hylian made and that some of them like  the ones in fahren could have been built  on top of older pre-existing ruins  there's definitely a case to be made  that these towers are indeed of highly  in origin despite the fact that four of  them are found on the outskirts of  farren the majority are actually located  in central hyrule close to the wetlands  in the age of calamity dlc we are given  the opportunity to visit gopanga village  a hylian settlement situated in the  wetlands and which was destroyed by  ganon's army in breath the wild's  timeline there's only two towers left  standing in the wetlands themselves in  breath the wild but as you can see in  age of calamity there were actually a  lot more of them all across the village  and not only are these in pristine  condition without moss and ivy covering  them but they still feature that same  hylian crest even if you don't accept  age of calamity as canon whatsoever it's  still a bit strange that the majority of  these towers are found in central hyrule  which is not considered to be backstreet  boy territory by any means there's no  other ruins related to them in this part  of the world and on top of that places  that do like taiflo ruins for example  don't feature any of these towers but as  is often the case with zelda theories  there's also a different side to the  story things that contradict the hylian  tower idea first is the obvious fact  that despite the inconsistency in the  decorations creating a champion does  still refer to them as zonai towers  regardless and second there's one  specific tower whose location raises a  lot of questions this outlier is found  inside the hebra mountain range it's  already a bit unusual to find them in  such a remote location but what's even  more strange is that this one is half  submerged in the middle of a lake this  implies that it was built before the  lake was formed and also means that this  entire waterfall probably didn't exist  yet which i can imagine is a very long  time ago while there are ancient hylian  structures that are as old if not older  than those made by the backstreet boys  the decorations on these towers are  modern hylian not ancient hylian ancient  hylian ruins have ornaments in crests of  their own some directly copied over from  skyward sword which is a neat little  touch and well as you can see none of  them match with the ones from the towers  instead the tower crest falls in line  with the style seen at hyrule castle  which i consider to be modern hylian  it's also worth noting that the hylians  weren't really all that active in the  hebra mountains aside from a wooden  cabin which looks to have been built  post calamity their closest settlement  was tabanta village which is still a  long ways away from the mountain range  at the very least we can say that the  hylians didn't have any stonework in  this area no garrisons or statues or  anything like that but you know who did  the backstreet boys not only do we find  one of their mazes here but they also  constructed two stone doors leading into  the mountains which feature their  recognizable serpent engraving so there  was definitely some activity here all  this conflicting evidence makes it kinda  hard to put a definitive stamp on who  was responsible for the construction of  the towers but you know what it's very  much possible that none of this even  matters because the more i looked into  it the more i get the impression that  the towers we ended up getting in breath  the wild are not the ones nintendo  initially wanted to include in the game  and are instead quick and dirty  replacements i find it highly suspicious  that not a single design we find of them  in creating a champion even comes close  to what we ultimately see in game they  are much more detailed and as mentioned  before they all have a clear motif  related to dragons now a lot of the  concept art in the book actually  features notes from who i presume to be  one of the lead artists most of these  are feedback and requests to make  certain changes and one of the artworks  has these types of notes attached to it  asking the artist to change some of the  details it really seems like they had a  pretty clear idea of what they wanted  the towers to look like so how did we go  from this a fully detailed dragon style  tower which actually coincides with the  building style of the tribe who made it  to this a boring pillar with zero  connection to dragons and a crest on it  that doesn't even belong of course the  easiest explanation would be that they  simply ran out of time and took a  pre-existing model changed it up a bit  and slapped it into the game as a  replacement the 3d modeler responsible  may have even forgotten to replace the  texture hence why the hylian crest is  still there alternatively they could  have concluded that the fancy design  seen in the concept art would stand out  too much and detract from the shika  towers i mean it's clear from the size  comparison alone that they were supposed  to be a whole lot bigger than the ones  we ended up getting but what if there  was a different reason what if they left  out this design because they wanted to  save it for a future story implication  perhaps dlc which may i remind you  breath the wild 2 was initially intended  to be there's several hints that breath  202 story events will have some sort of  connection to the ancient dragons as i  discussed in my previous video they  often disappear into a portal in the sky  and in the sequel we see a sky realm  that seems to be invisible from the  surface at the end of the second teaser  zelda's lullaby is played by the same  instrument used for the dragon's music  theme then we have these enigmatic robot  creatures who also feature elements of  dragons and of course has mentioned  before all the zonai related stuff a  tribe who had a clear fascination with  the ancient dragons particularly farage  who makes frequent appearances in the  farren region and yes i'm calling them  zonai again from now i think the joke  has kind of run its course anyway what  i'm trying to propose is that the zonai  were well aware of the sky portals as  well as the existence of the skyroam and  they themselves may have even found a  way to travel between the surface and  the heavens by constructing magical  towers not only are the zonai described  as having been powerful magic wielders  but the description of the towers  themselves state that they said to have  been used for magic purposes a statement  like this doesn't just come out of  nowhere and in fact nothing in the  actual game suggests that the towers had  magical properties for all we know they  were simply yet another ancient ruin  with a chest on top and nothing else we  know that the writers of creating a  champion were given a pretty extensive  insight into the ideas and thought  process of the zelda team it's how they  got access to all this concept art notes  as well as quotes from the developers  themselves in fact the book reveals  quite a lot of details that are never  actually seen or mentioned in the game  itself and couldn't possibly have been  known unless the zelda team itself  informed the writers about it like how  the guardians emerged from the columns  at hyrule castle during the calamity an  idea which was actually used in age of  calamity two years after the book was  published as such i think it's plausible  that the zelda team had bigger plans for  actual magic zonai towers but weren't  able to implement them because of either  time restraints or because they simply  didn't fit brethwald's story at the time  and might have been put on the shelf for  later story wise i personally think they  would be very fitting i find it quite  fascinating how the original tower  designs depict not only dragons but  specifically dragons pointing up towards  the sky almost as a representation of  their ascent into the heavens the zonai  could have constructed these towers not  just to honor the dragons but also with  the purpose of traveling to the heavenly  realm and the so-called magic they used  could be related to link's new ability  seen in the second teaser where he  ascends rapidly and then phases through  the floor of one of the floating islands  i actually made an entire video devoted  to this mechanic where i explained some  of the details based on information  inside one of the patents issued by  nintendo inside the patent it says that  in some specific scenarios the ability  can be used to reach locations very very  high up basically without a height limit  i theorize that this is how we'll be  able to travel between the surface and  the islands in the sky and i also  mentioned that there might be something  akin to pedestals on the surface by  which we can do this well what if these  towers are going to be exactly that i  noticed that one of the designs has a  disc shaped platform on top divided into  rings and i don't know about you but to  me this looks eerily similar to the  platform we see links standing on in the  new footage here too we see a circular  floor design with multiple rings also  notice how in the background we don't  see clouds or a blue sky but rather what  seems to be a landscape it's obviously  very blurry due to the camera's focus  and it could very well be one of the sky  islands but what if this platform isn't  in the sky but instead link is standing  on top of one of these new zonai towers  on the surface and it's from here that  he'll be able to use his new ability to  travel further up into the skyrim of  course that does beg the question if  these towers do indeed exist where are  they why don't we see them in breath of  the wild nor in the sequel footage well  the latter is quite obvious since  nintendo is known to hide or emit  certain things from their promotional  material i mean just look at how they  purposely left out terraco from the  first age of calamity trailer as for why  they weren't in breath the wild well my  best guess would be that they are  probably hidden on the ground similar to  the shika towers and that at some point  in the story they will emerge from the  earth either all of them simultaneously  or maybe we need to activate them one by  one it could even be one of the  objectives of going on the ground to  begin with by traveling below ground and  activating a new tower there it'll rise  up to the surface and doing so will  grant access to new islands in the sky  which were previously unreachable not  only would it be a great way to connect  the underground surface and sky but it  also allows the developers to obstruct  certain parts of the sky in a natural  way a way for the player to unlock new  areas bit by bit instead of making every  location accessible from the get-go like  in breath of the wild so to recap i  believe that these are not the quote  unquote real zonai towers and that the  ones we see in creating a champion are  and might show up in the sequel as both  a replacement for the shika towers as  well as a way to travel between the  surface and the sky if this ends up  being true it would be yet another case  where nintendo's future plans are hidden  inside their concept art just like we  see with link's arm as well as the  broken master sword anyway that's enough  zone i for one video i want to quickly  let you all know that in the coming days  i'll be making a community post in which  i will describe the details about the  100k subscribers special which as always  will have audience participation i'm  running a bit behind on it so i  apologize for that but i really wanted  to make this video first now that that's  done i will be working on the special  starting next week so i hope you look  forward to that again be sure to check  out the community post if you'd like to  have a chance to join in a big thanks as  always to my discord mods and to those  who support the channel financially you  are all the best and that is all for now  this is dawn signing off and have a good  one  [Music]  you

